   "fix": "Rename `weight_mul` \u2192 `weight_mul_apply` and `weight_mul'` \u2192 `weight_mul`, and update the four uses (`simp_rw [\u2190 weight_mul]` line 158; `rw [\u2190 weight_mul']` lines 218, 245, 375) and the module docstring reference at line 31.",
   "issue": "`weight_mul` (line 96) is the applied form `weight (f * O) g x = weight f g x * O x` while `weight_mul'` (line 102) is the function-level `weight (f * O) g = weight f g * O` \u2014 the reverse of the adjacent `weight_abs_apply` (line 107, applied) / `weight_abs` (line 112, function-level) pair, and of `weight_apply` (line 91). A user who learned `weight_abs_apply` will guess `weight_mul_apply` and find nothing, while `weight_mul` silently delivers the applied form.",
   "line": 96
  }
